# zView source pin for sdk/zview/build-zview.sh (TASK/ZVIEW-M4).
#
# z-tools-04805b7.tar.xz = a subset of the z-tools repository at commit
#   04805b77d6fc246ee507c8c5e2317b58b1a531e4 (2024-09-12, "Update README.md")
#   of https://github.com/mikrosk/z-tools (zView 1.0.1 LDG version, Zorro /
#   Miro Kropacek), checked out in Applications/z-tools. Made with
#     git archive --format=tar --prefix=z-tools-04805b7/ 04805b7 \
#       README.md prerequisites.txt common.mak common zview \
#       ztask/gmem.c ztask/gmem.h \
#       ':(exclude)zview/_dist/fonts' ':(exclude)zview/_dist/goodies' \
#       ':(exclude)zview/_dist/doc/hypview' | xz -9e
#   (xz 5.8.3). Every file in it is byte-identical to the commit. Left out:
#   the PDF fonts (zview/_dist/fonts, xpdf only), third-party goodies
#   (m68k binaries) and the HypView viewer -- none is built or installed.
#   ztask/gmem.{c,h} are in because zView's sources include "gmem.h" and call
#   gmalloc/grealloc/gfree, which its own build takes from xpdf's goo library
#   (zview/Makefile:12-15,35); xpdf is the PDF module NewTOS leaves out, and
#   z-tools' own C version of that API (ztask/gmem.c, same authors, same
#   repository) stands in for it unchanged.
#
